NOTICE — provenance of the contents of this repository
======================================================

This repository is a Guix channel. Most of what it contains is code written for
it; the parts that come from elsewhere are listed here, with their licence.


Kernel source (rpi/kernel.scm)
------------------------------

The kernel is the Raspberry Pi downstream tree, fetched as a release tarball:

  https://github.com/raspberrypi/linux  tag stable_20250916  (Linux 6.12.47)

That tree is GPL-2.0-only. It is fetched, never vendored: no kernel source is
stored in this repository, and no patch is applied here — a board that needs one
passes its own patch list to the constructor and carries those patches itself.

The Guix package code around it (rpi/kernel.scm, rpi/firmware.scm,
rpi/image.scm, rpi/bootloader.scm, rpi-boot-populate) is GPL-3.0-or-later, like
the rest of this repository. See LICENSE.


Firmware (rpi/firmware.scm)
---------------------------

Three items are installed from other projects. None of them is redistributed
here: each package fetches or copies from its own source at build time.

  brcmfmac43455 files       extracted from linux-firmware
                            (https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/
                            firmware/linux-firmware.git), whose licence is the
                            per-file one; the Broadcom blobs are non-free and are
                            distributed for use with the hardware they ship with.
                            linux-firmware is provided by the nonguix channel,
                            not by Guix.

  BCM4345C0.hcd             https://github.com/RPi-Distro/bluez-firmware,
                            Broadcom Bluetooth firmware, non-free, same terms.

  regulatory.db(.p7s)       wireless-regdb
                            (https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/
                            linville/wireless-regdb.git), ISC-like licence; the
                            file is generated from db.txt by a free tool.

Because of these three, the channel declares nonguix as a dependency. A
repository that carried them itself would be redistributing non-free blobs;
this one only points at their sources.


Boot template (rpi/boot/config.txt)
-----------------------------------

Written for this channel from the documented behaviour of the Raspberry Pi
firmware. No vendor file is copied into it.
